    `WrapEllipsoid::findClosestPoint` and `closestPointToEllipse` are in turn
    David Eberly's point-to-ellipsoid and point-to-ellipse algorithms from
    Graphics Gems IV, as noted in OpenSim's own source.

The port is not a verbatim copy: it computes the wrapped path's scalar LENGTH
only, does not return the wrap points OpenSim generates for rendering, and
implements only the `hybrid` ellipsoid method. Every intentional difference is
listed under DEVIATIONS at the top of `MusclePathWrap.cpp`.

`BioMotion/Resources/FullBody.osim` and `BioMotion/Resources/Rajagopal2016.osim`
are OpenSim musculoskeletal models; their own licence terms are recorded in
STATUS.md ("The upper-limb licence blocker").

